{"schema":"body-shape-lookup/1","rig":"mixamo-106","row":"body -> [shapeIndex, height_mm, girth_x100, mass_kg_x10, unclamped_mass_kg_x10]; shape = shapes[shapeIndex]; radius_m = map.r * height_m * girth; role mass_kg = map.m * mass. Girth is the body's own radius scale against its shape (a heavy MakeHuman body in an average shape reads 1.3, say). Use bodyShape(lookup, id) from src/shape-maps.mjs: it throws for an unknown or excluded id.","rules":{"child_max_height_mm":1450,"child":"Height under 1450 mm is the child shape, whatever the build: a small adult under 1.45 m (e.g. mon-0056, 1445 mm) becomes a child, and mon-0846 at 1462 mm is average-heavy. The height is the only input; there is no age field in the measure rows.","mass":"mass_kg_x10 is the role table's mass clamped to 18..140 kg (the role table's bounds), so it reads exactly 140 for 193 of 578 bodies (and 18 for 1). The 5th value is the unclamped volume-based mass: use it to scale impulses. The clamp is deliberate for ragdoll joint stiffness, not a measurement.","excluded":"Scale outliers (height under 1.0 m or over 3.0 m) have no shape: bodyShape throws."},"shapes":["child","average-medium","average-heavy","tall-medium","giant-slim","giant-massive","giant-heavy"],"excluded":{"pirate-by-p-konstantinov":"scale outlier: height 647 mm from a GLB node-scale error, not a body; no shape (re-measure the GLB and rerun)","the-boss":"scale outlier: height 538 mm from a GLB node-scale error, not a body; no shape (re-measure the GLB and rerun)","remy":"scale outlier: height 3650 mm from a GLB node-scale error, not a body; no shape (re-measure the GLB and rerun)"},"bodies":{
